Z||000006||Fiero5||06-04-2001||03:30 PM||||"Awesome! how do you get those colors to come out of your sunroof like that?!"<P>Taken from the "Fiero history" web site:<BR>Fiero history;<BR>.. the man who brought the Fiero from paper<BR>to production was Hulki Aldikacti. After working on a few unique features, ...  <A HREF="http://www.Pontiacfiero/history.html " TARGET=_blank>http://www.Pontiacfiero/history.html </A> <BR>"The optional "rainbow" emitters in some models of GM's inovative mid engine Pontiac Fiero use state of the art technology developed at Entech. GM used a dual laser set-up to shoot a micro laser that was projected from an intergrated flow "horn" built into a section of the large sunroof panel. These emitters would split the lasers into two coherent beams of photons. The laser emitters being housed within the special sunroof panel which contains the photon displacement tubing, could in effect project a man made rainbow out into the air from the special enhanced glass. The special emitter design was made so if these laser beams cross inside a type of a nonlinear crystal, they mutually influence each others propagation. In some cases, one beam will donate its photons to the other beam. This results in nonreciprocal energy transfer between the beams, and constitutes one of the few instances of optical amplification without stimulated emission."<P>The control of light by light is the optical analog of the control of electrons by electrons in transistors. One of the great challenges facing quantum optics today is the search for the appropriate medium in which photons can control photons. The discovery of such a medium would open the way for photonic<BR>computers.<P>Steve<P>------------------<BR>                        <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Fiero9-86SS1.jpg">                        <BR>http://www.kelleyfamilyfieros.homestead.com/index.html||||reg||12
